## Summary
The article reports that Ebola deaths in the Democratic Republic of Congo are nearing 2,700, with 5,514 confirmed cases and 2,642 deaths. The World Health Organization has warned that this is the fastest-growing outbreak in the nation's history.

## Key Points
- 5,514 confirmed cases of Ebola in DR Congo.
- 2,642 deaths attributed to the outbreak.
- This is described as the fastest-growing Ebola outbreak in DR Congo's history.
- The World Health Organization has issued a warning about the severity.


